  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The correct order of acid strengths of benzoic acid $(X),$ peroxybenzoic acid $(Y)$ and $p$-nitrobenzoic acid $(Z)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "2XJIH",
      "text": "$Y>Z>X$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "RpWm8",
      "text": "$Z>Y>X$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "m3zQU",
      "text": "$Z>X>Y$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "SNpCo",
      "text": "$Y>X>Z$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\because$ In $p$ -nitrobenzoic acid $(Z)-\\mathrm{NO}_{2}$ present as electron withdrawing group, thus is most acidic\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2017_che_a60.png\">\r\n\r\n$(X) \\because$ Benzoic acid is stabilised via resonance, thus is more acidic than per oxybenzoic acid.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2017_che_a60a.png\">\r\n\r\n(Y) peroxy benzoic acid does not show any such resonance.<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2017_che_a60b.png\">\r\n\r\nThus is least acidic.\r\nHence, correct order is $Z>X>Y$",
    "image": null
  },
